# The native ppc64le D3D11 lane: this module is DXVK behind a COM thunk, the
# same shape as dlls/d3d12 and vkd3d-proton.  See dlls/d3d11/main.c.
#
# Wine's own wined3d-backed implementation (async.c, buffer.c, d3d11_main.c,
# decoder.c, device.c, inputlayout.c, shader.c, state.c, texture.c, utils.c,
# view.c) is deliberately LEFT IN THE TREE and dropped from SOURCES rather
# than deleted: it is upstream Wine's, unmodified, and keeping it unbuilt
# makes this lane a reversible change to one file instead of a 19,000-line
# deletion to review.  Nothing links it.
#
# win32u is imported by the PE side, not linked by the unixlib: the PE half
# answers DXVK's two questions about a window (its client size, and whether it
# still exists) with NtUserGetClientRect/NtUserIsWindow on the application's
# own thread and pushes the answers down.  The unixlib deliberately does NOT
# link -lwin32u -- see the note in ../d3d12/unix_win32u.c about the DT_NEEDED a
# headless build tree cannot satisfy.
MODULE    = d3d11.dll
UNIXLIB   = d3d11.so
IMPORTLIB = d3d11
IMPORTS   = winecom win32u
UNIX_LIBS = $(PTHREAD_LIBS)
# ppc64le/dxvk holds the ONE copy of the WSI callback ABI the DXVK patch
# series and dlls/d3d11/unix.c both compile against.
#
# BOTH VARIABLES, AND THE SAME PATH IN EACH, which is what dlls/d3d12 does and
# is not redundancy.  makedep uses them for different things (tools/makedep.c):
# EXTRAINCL's -I entries go into include_paths, which is how makedep RESOLVES
# the #include while generating dependencies, and UNIX_CFLAGS is what actually
# reaches the compiler for a unix source.  [MEASURED] with UNIX_CFLAGS alone,
# makedep fails with "dxvk_win32u_wsi.h: No such file or directory" and leaves
# the Makefile unregenerated -- so the build then compiles with a STALE
# Makefile and the failure looks like the flag was ignored.  With EXTRAINCL
# alone, makedep is happy and the compile line has no -I at all.
EXTRAINCL   = -I$(srcdir)/../../ppc64le/dxvk
UNIX_CFLAGS = -I$(srcdir)/../../ppc64le/dxvk

VER_FILEDESCRIPTION_STR = "Wine Direct3D"
VER_PRODUCTVERSION      = 7,0,6002,18107

SOURCES = \
	d3d11.thunks \
	main.c \
	unix.c \
	unix_win32u.c
